    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01JMFXB80MWN6EVETABXXVCGGX\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to change your notification settings for new tickets in Klaviyo Helpdesk. You can enable notifications to help you keep track of new tickets.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JMFXB80MYZ0TQVWPZS295BJ6\">Types of notifications</h2>\n<p>There are 2 types of notifications you can choose:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Email notifications</li>\n<li>Unread conversations badge</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"h_01K09WBC36PECQGKYKAWP1065V\">Email notifications</h3>\n<p>If you'd like to be notified via an email notification when you receive new ticket in Helpdesk, you can enable email notifications. This setting is off by default. </p>\n<p>If you choose to enable these email notifications, you must set at least 1 recipient; however, you can add any number of email addresses.</p>\n<p>Recommendation: turn this setting on if you use Helpdesk to manage your customer support communications; otherwise, leave this setting off. </p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01K09V9N8VC1NHZ9NJJVHZSQAW\">Turn on email notifications</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Service &gt; Helpdesk</strong> in Klaviyo's main navigation menu.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Settings</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39046127100827\" alt=\"Inboxsettings.jpg\" width=\"250\" height=\"315\">\n</li>\n<li>Select the <strong>Inbound messages</strong> tab in the top menu bar.</li>\n<li>Under <em>Email notifications</em>, toggle the setting <strong>On</strong>.</li>\n<li>Add the email addresses you want the notifications to send to.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39046135540251\" alt=\"inboxnotifications1.jpg\" width=\"423\" height=\"263\">\n</li>\n<li>Optional: Click the dropdown arrow to add another email address, then select <strong>Add email</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"h_01K09WBC36N3S9ECD0AHR0H3QR\">Unread conversations badge</h3>\n<p>The unread conversations badge setting is on by default. This setting, when enabled, displays a red badge on the Helpdesk tab in Klaviyo's main navigation with a count of your unopened tickets.</p>\n<p>Note that the count is based on a ticket-level per profile, not by the number of messages. For example, if person A texts you 3 times, the badge will show only 1 unread ticket. If persons A, B, and C each text you 1 time, the badge will show 3 unread tickets. </p>\n<p>Recommendation: leave this setting on so you can monitor the number of tickets coming in.</p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01K09VZNSCCMXXK33ZXQDZ3ASP\">Disable unread conversations badge</h4>\n<ol>\n<li>Go to <strong>Service &gt; Helpdesk </strong>in Klaviyo's main navigation menu.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Settings</strong>.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/39046127100827\" alt=\"Inboxsettings.jpg\" width=\"276\" height=\"348\">\n</li>\n<li>Select the <strong>General</strong> tab in the menu bar at the top.</li>\n<li>Under <em>Unread conversation notifications</em>, click <strong>Off</strong>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save</strong>. The unread conversations badge will no longer show in Klaviyo's navigation.</li>\n</ol>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
